virglrenderer: set the legacy vertex state and select shaders only when they change

What: on a GL without ARB_vertex_attrib_binding (Apple's OpenGL 4.1),
vrend_draw_bind_vertex_legacy now clears vbo_dirty like the GL 4.3 path does, so
vrend_draw_vbo selects the shaders only when something marked them dirty. Per sub
context it records what the last legacy vertex setup gave its VAO (program and
vrend_program_bind_gen, vertex elements, each element's buffer name, stride and
offset, the enabled mask) and skips the attribute loop when all of it is the same;
an attribute with stride 0 (its value is read from the buffer on every draw) is
never skipped. The element buffer is bound only when another one is asked for.
vrend_vertex_state_gen drops every record when the VAO may have changed outside
the draw path: an index buffer bound to its own target (transfers, map, create),
a buffer deleted (its GL name can come back for another buffer), vertex elements
freed, a video command. A draw whose setup the GL refused keeps no record.
Shader key audit (the selects on every draw hid these): unbinding the vertex
elements or the rasterizer, a framebuffer change that stops half way, and a
sampler view slot whose key bits (emulated rectangle, buffer swizzle) change now
mark the shaders dirty; a freed program selects again.
OMACVM_VIRGL_SELECT_CACHE=0 leaves vbo_dirty set (shaders selected on every draw),
OMACVM_VIRGL_VERTEX_CACHE=0 sets attributes and element buffer on every draw;
both 0 send the GL calls of before. Each logs one line at start.
OMACVM_VIRGL_CACHE_STATS=1 logs draws, selects and skips every 10 s and when a
context ends.
Why: WebGL Aquarium draws one fish per draw call (~31k draws a frame at 30k fish)
and the render thread is the limit (~1.37 us per draw on an M4). Every draw selected
the shaders again (3 key fills and compares, 6 % of the thread) and sent
glBindBuffer + glVertexAttrib*Pointer + glVertexAttribDivisor for every attribute
(4 %), after which Apple's GL rebuilds its vertex array state in the draw (part of
11 %). Linux hosts with GL 4.3 already select only when dirty.
Upstream: upstream behaviour on the legacy path; upstreamable; not sent.
Test: Tests/virgl/test-vertex-binds.c (run as is and with each switch at 0) and
the static check in Tests/virgl/run-regressions.py (every GL call that changes VAO
state or frees a buffer must tell the cache or be reviewed).

