+/* OmacVM: bumped whenever the VAO state of some sub context may have changed outside
+ * the draw path: an index buffer bound to its own target for a transfer (that is the
+ * bound VAO's element buffer binding), a buffer deleted (its GL name can come back for
+ * another buffer, while a VAO that was not current still points at the old one), vertex
+ * elements freed (their address can come back), a video command. It makes every sub
+ * context's recorded vertex setup and element buffer binding stale. Starts at 1 so a
+ * zeroed sub context never matches; 64 bits never wrap. Render thread only. */
+static uint64_t vrend_vertex_state_gen = 1;
